    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Question\n\nI installed with lazy.nvim package manager, but on typing, I don't get any completion.\r\n\r\nI can see language servers are running, for each different language, and mini.completion is installed (`:Lazy` shows it is).",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I installed with lazy.nvim package manager, but on typing, I don't get any completion.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I can see language servers are running, for each different language, and mini.completion is installed (<code class=\"notranslate\">:Lazy</code> shows it is).</p>",
